      "body_markdown": "Roughly 97 per cent of all the water on Earth sits in the salty oceans, yet the rain that fills our rivers is fresh and clean. How does that happen? The answer is a giant, never-ending journey called the water cycle, and it is driven entirely by heat from the sun. Each day the sun warms the surface of seas, lakes and rivers, and this heat turns some of the liquid water into an invisible gas known as water vapour.\n\nThis first step has a name: *evaporation*. The warm water vapour is lighter than the air around it, so it rises upwards into the cooler air high above the ground. As it climbs, it slowly loses its heat. When the vapour becomes cold enough, it changes back into tiny drops of water, far too small to see clearly on their own. Scientists call this change *condensation*.\n\nThese tiny drops do not stay alone. Millions of them join together, and that is exactly what a cloud is — a vast crowd of water droplets floating in the sky. For a while the air is able to hold them up. But the drops keep bumping into one another and growing larger and heavier, and the air cannot support them forever.\n\nEventually the drops become so heavy that they fall to the ground as rain, which scientists call *precipitation*. The water then flows across the land into streams and rivers, and most of it returns at last to the sea. There the sun is waiting to warm it once more, and the whole cycle begins again. How much rain any single region receives in a year, however, remains hard to predict with certainty.",
      "metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "Khi câu hỏi hỏi 'cái gì gây ra / điều khiển X', hãy tìm cụm 'by + N' trong câu bị động — đó thường là đáp án ('the sun').",
            "point": "Bị động CÓ nêu tác nhân 'by' (be + V3 + by O)",
            "review": "Bị động: S + be + V3 + by O. Giữ 'by…' khi tác nhân quan trọng; lược bỏ khi không cần thiết.",
            "example": "it **is driven** entirely **by** heat from the sun",
            "analysis": "'is driven by heat from the sun' = bị động hiện tại đơn nhưng GIỮ lại tác nhân sau 'by' vì 'heat from the sun' chính là thông tin quan trọng nhất (cái vận hành vòng tuần hoàn). Khác bị động thường lược bỏ 'by…'."
