      "library": "l1_vocab",
      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "## Keeping Your Teeth Healthy\n\nA **tooth** may look simple, but it is covered by **enamel**, the hardest material in the human body. Even so, this strong layer can be damaged if it is not looked after.\n\nThe main danger comes from **sugar**. When you eat sweet food, tiny **bacteria** in your mouth feed on the sugar. As they do this, they make **acid**. Over time, this acid attacks the enamel and causes tooth **decay**. Decay leads to holes and pain.\n\nThe good news is that simple habits help. You should **brush** your teeth gently twice a day. Most toothpaste contains **fluoride**. This chemical makes the enamel stronger and helps fight decay. Eating less sugar also keeps your teeth in better shape.\n\nIt is also wise to see a **dentist** for a regular **check-up**. A dentist can find a small problem before it grows. With a little daily care, most people can keep their teeth healthy for life.",
