      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "Do you feel **tired** in the afternoon? You are not alone. Many people feel sleepy\nafter lunch. A short **nap** can help.\n\nA nap is a short sleep in the day. It is not a long sleep at night. When you are\nsleepy, your **brain** works slowly. You cannot **focus**, and you make more\n**mistakes**. A small sleep can fix this.\n\nNew **research** shows that the best naps are short — about 20 minutes. After a\n20-minute nap, most people feel **refreshed**. They have more **energy**, and they\ncan think clearly again. A nap can also help your **memory**. While you sleep, your\nbrain saves the things you learned.\n\nBut be careful. A very long nap can make you feel worse, not better. You may feel\nsleepy when you wake up. So keep your nap short. Twenty minutes is enough to feel\n**awake** and ready again.",
