    {
      "id": "ba9aa21c-4b5b-5c5a-b69a-2d1d89bbb26f",
      "slug": "the-rise-of-electric-cars",
      "title": "The Rise of Electric Cars",
      "library": "l1_vocab",
      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "In 2023, close to one in five new cars sold worldwide ran on electricity rather\nthan petrol — about 18 percent, according to the International Energy Agency — a\nshare that would have seemed impossible only a decade earlier. The\nelectric vehicle, once a curiosity, has moved firmly into the mainstream, and the\nreasons behind its rise reveal as much about politics as about engineering.\n\nThe central appeal is environmental. A traditional **combustion** engine burns fuel\nand **emits** carbon dioxide and other pollutants directly into the air. An electric\nmotor, by contrast, produces no **emissions** while it is being driven, which makes it\nattractive to cities struggling with dirty air. Drivers simply **charge** the battery\nat home or at a public station, and improvements in battery technology have steadily\nextended the **range** a car can travel on a single charge.\n\nYet the transition is far from simple. Charging **infrastructure** remains uneven,\nthin in the countryside even where it is dense in cities. Prices, although falling,\nare still high, so many governments offer a **subsidy** to encourage buyers to\n**adopt** the technology sooner.\n\nDeeper questions also remain. If millions of vehicles draw power from an electricity\n**grid** that still burns coal or gas, the climate benefit shrinks. The real gain\narrives only when that grid is supplied by **renewable** sources such as wind and\nsolar. Manufacturing creates further concerns, because companies must **extract**\nmetals such as lithium and cobalt, a process that can damage local environments.\n\nNone of these problems has stopped the momentum. Several governments have announced\nplans to **phase out** the sale of new petrol cars within the coming decade, and\nmanufacturers are investing heavily to meet the deadline. Whether cost and the\nremaining **barriers** can be removed quickly enough to match these ambitions is a\nquestion that the next few years are likely to answer.",
      "metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "Bị động tiếp diễn nhấn vào quá trình đang diễn ra; chú ý phân biệt với bị động đơn (trạng thái/sự thật chung).",
            "point": "Bị động hiện tại tiếp diễn + lược tác nhân",
            "review": "Bị động tiếp diễn: S + is/are + being + V3. 'while + clause' chỉ thời gian song song.",
            "example": "An electric motor… produces no emissions **while it is being driven**",
            "analysis": "'is being driven' là bị động hiện tại tiếp diễn (is + being + V3) trong mệnh đề thời gian 'while + S + V'. Tác nhân (người lái) bị lược vì trọng tâm là trạng thái 'đang được lái'. 'while' ở đây chỉ thời gian (= trong lúc)."
