      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "What do you wash your hands with? Most people use **soap**. But where does soap come\nfrom? Its story is very old, much older than you may think.\n\n**Ancient** people made soap from about 2800 BC. The Babylonians were some of the\nfirst. They used **fat** and **ash** to make it. They would **boil** the fat in water.\nThen they added wood ash to the pot. This **mix** of fat and ash could **clean** things\nvery well.\n\nAt first, people did not use soap to wash their bodies. They used it to clean wool and\ncloth in their homes. Later, people saw that soap was also gentle on the **skin**. So\nthey began to wash their hands and bodies with it every day.\n\nToday, soap is **cheap** and easy to buy in any shop. But it is still made from the same\nold ideas from long ago.",
