    {
      "id": "bc4c5a76-a4fe-55ed-a93d-1d086a6a791a",
      "slug": "why-we-need-museums",
      "title": "Why We Need Museums",
      "library": "l1_vocab",
      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "Every year, more than eight million people walk through the Louvre in Paris to stand\nbefore a small painting of a smiling woman. The Mona Lisa is just one of millions of\n**object**s that museums around the world protect for everyone.\n\nThe word \"museum\" comes from the Muses, the Greek goddesses of art and learning. For a\nlong time, rich families kept **rare** objects in **private** rooms. Only in the 1700s\ndid the first **public** museums open their doors, letting ordinary visitors see\n**treasure**s that were once hidden away.\n\nA good museum does much more than **display** old things behind glass. Skilled staff\nclean, repair, and store **fragile** items so they survive for future **generation**s.\n**Curator**s arrange each **exhibit** to tell a clear story, and labels explain what\nvisitors are looking at. Schools bring children to learn through real objects rather\nthan pictures in a book. In this way a single visit can teach more than many lessons.\n\nMuseums are not free of **debate**. Some of their most famous objects were taken from\nother countries long ago, and many nations now ask for them back. A few large museums\nhave already returned treasures to their original homes. As these arguments continue,\nthe **role** of the modern museum may keep changing for years to come.",
      "metadata": {
        "grammar_focus": [
          {
            "tip": "Mệnh đề quan hệ thường giấu thông tin chính; xác định nó bổ nghĩa cho danh từ nào để trả lời câu hỏi chi tiết.",
            "point": "Mệnh đề quan hệ xác định với 'that'",
            "review": "Mệnh đề quan hệ xác định: N + who/which/that + (S) + V… , không dùng dấu phẩy. 'that' dùng cho cả người và vật.",
            "example": "The Mona Lisa is just one of millions of objects **that museums around the world protect** for everyone.",
            "analysis": "'that' thay cho 'objects' và mở đầu mệnh đề quan hệ xác định, cho biết đó là những hiện vật nào. Không có dấu phẩy trước 'that' vì mệnh đề cần thiết để giới hạn nghĩa. Bên trong, 'museums' là chủ ngữ, 'protect' là động từ."
