      "title": "Why We Yawn",
      "library": "l1_vocab",
      "status": "published",
      "body_markdown": "Did you just **yawn** while reading this word? Yawning is very common, and everyone does\nit. But why do we yawn? Scientists are not fully sure.\n\nPeople yawn more when they are **tired** or bored. But a yawn may do something else too.\nOne idea is that yawning helps **cool** the **brain**. When the brain gets too **warm**,\na yawn may help bring it back down. A yawn brings a **deep** **breath** of air into your\nbody. This breath may help the brain cool down a little.\n\nThere is a strange thing about yawns too. You can **catch** a yawn from another person.\nWhen you see someone yawn, you often **copy** it without trying. You do not even think\nabout it at all.\n\nSo next time you yawn, look around at the people near you. Maybe your friend will yawn\nsoon too.",
